afk: rebuild a streamed tool card when its name grows after first surfacing.

Motivation: providers may stream a tool call whose name is still a partial
prefix when it first surfaces, growing in later cumulative updates while the
call id stays stable (llama.cpp's chat-diff streaming: compute_diffs
tolerates prefix->longer name transitions and the server mints the id at
first surfacing). ToolExecutionComponent binds its renderer to the name at
construction, so a card created under "wri" stays on the generic fallback
renderer and write/edit previews render blank until completion.

What must survive a rebase:
- A WeakMap (#pendingToolComponentNames) recording the name each pending
  component was created under, written at BOTH creation sites in
  #handleMessageUpdate: the read-group path and the ToolExecutionComponent
  path.
- The displacement check at the top of the toolCall loop body in
  #handleMessageUpdate (after the streamed-id re-key — since 18.6.0 done
  once by #reconcileStreamedToolCallIds before the loop — and before
  toolRenderName(content.name, tool)): if the pending component for
  content.id was created under a different name, remove it from the chat
  container (guarded by canRemoveBlock) and drop its
  pendingTools/#toolTimelineComponents entries so the normal creation path
  below rebuilds it under the settled name. It compares the RAW
  content.name (both creation sites store raw names).
- Two tests in test/modes/controllers/: event-controller-partial-name.test.ts
  (name rebind repro) and event-controller-openai-args.test.ts (throttle-
  parsed arguments still grow the write preview without partialJson).

Rebased 17.2.14 -> 18.0.11: upstream renamed the container guard to
canRemoveBlock (both the source hunk and the partial-name test's
chatContainer mock updated); creation sites and loop structure otherwise
match, offsets refreshed.

Rebased 18.1.13 -> 18.2.10: upstream added #settleHeldCompletionIfPresent
after the read-group registration; the displacement block sits above it
unchanged. The two tests import ToolExecutionComponent and initTheme
from @oh-my-pi/pi-tui (chat/tool-execution, theme) after the renderer
migration.

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream moved the per-index id re-key out
of the toolCall loop into #reconcileStreamedToolCallIds (called once
before the loop), so the `#streamedToolCallIdByIndex.set(...)` anchor is
gone. The displacement block now opens the loop body, right after the
`content.type !== "toolCall"` skip and before toolRenderName — still
after the id re-key, still comparing the raw content.name. Upstream does
not rebind on name growth itself; both creation sites carried over
unchanged. The two tests now build their context with upstream's shared
test/helpers/interactive-mode-context.ts (real TranscriptContainer,
settings-registry-backed reveal); the hand-rolled ctx stub no longer
satisfies cfg*.get(settings).

